// The animation state of the per-player message (PS3 1.19 anim pack body, b119): the actor's animation controller writes
// its command list (up to 0x2000 words), and that list goes into the bit stream in the PS3 layout:
//   flag 0, the actor's frame (with "attached to": flag, 13-bit net id, then the frame relative to that player), for a
//   player message (flags & 1) the camera frame, its 8-bit zoom and the aim vector; then the animation table: count
//   (5 bits), "every command its own entry" (1 bit), 12-bit indexes, the art-group tabs (one shared 3-bit tab, or one
//   each; 7 = a 32-bit id follows); then the commands: 2-bit kinds with their extra bits (animations with their phase in
//   4 / 8 / 16 bits by frame count, snapshots, "none", blends with direction / mode / weight, blend-to-previous), layer
//   marks, and the end (3, 1).
// Layers (marks 0x19) the C side doesn't count are skipped; only the first `max_count` commands of a counted layer
// (counts 0x1a) go out. Refused (0 returned, ec counters): no actor or tabs (66), no controller, no command buffer (74),
// no camera for a player (68), an animation not in the actor's art groups (75 / 76), too many entries (70). ec[67]
// attachment without its character, ec[69] inconsistent commands. The "packing" byte base+0x16e79f0 is set meanwhile.
